{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01YaSEYxVoxD7o8mAphhMXt8", "type": "tool_result", "content": "Web search results for query: \"gpui rust ui framework\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"github.com\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Glass-HQ/gpui\"},{\"title\":\"gpui component\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/longbridge/gpui-component\"},{\"title\":\"gpui kit\",\"url\":\"https://libraries.io/cargo/gpui-kit\"},{\"title\":\"gpui framework\",\"url\":\"https://www.mintlify.com/Glass-HQ/Glass/reference/gpui-framework\"},{\"title\":\"github.com\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/blob/main/crates/gpui/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"Expand description\",\"url\":\"https://docs.rs/gpui\"},{\"title\":\"Expand description\",\"url\":\"https://docs.rs/gpui-pre/=0.3.7/\"},{\"title\":\"guise-ui 1.0.0\",\"url\":\"https://docs.rs/crate/guise-ui/1.0.0\"},{\"title\":\"Expand description\",\"url\":\"https://docs.rs/gpui-pre/=0.3.5/\"},{\"title\":\"gpui.rs\",\"url\":\"https://gpui.rs/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about GPUI:\n\n## Overview\n\nGPUI is a hybrid immediate and retained mode, GPU accelerated, UI framework for Rust, designed to support a wide variety of applications. It's a fast, productive UI framework for Rust from the creators of Zed.\n\n## Current Status\n\nGPUI is still in active development as we work on the Zed code editor, and is still pre-1.0. There will often be breaking changes between versions. You'll need to use the latest version of stable Rust and be on macOS or Linux.\n\n## Key Features\n\n- **Rendering**: GPUI is a custom GPU-accelerated UI framework that provides cross-platform rendering using Metal, DirectX, or Vulkan, reactive state management with entity-based architecture, and high performance with minimal allocations and efficient updates.\n\n- **Element Control**: Elements have total control over how they and their child elements are rendered and can be used for making efficient views into large lists, implement custom layouting for a code editor, and anything else you can think of.\n\n## Getting Started\n\nYou can create an application with Application::new(), and kick off your application by passing a callback to Application::run(). Inside this callback, you can create a new window with App::open_window(), and register your first root view.\n\nThere are also related frameworks and component libraries built on GPUI, such as GPUI Component and guise-ui, which provide additional pre-built UI components.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "be678a48-b318-40c8-b555-1fc4cdfd2ce6", "uuid": "c061c06c-6c09-4171-8b0f-d0b0200dc7c4", "timestamp": "2026-10-09T17:56:54.601Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "gpui rust ui framework", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_014KtmUyzEL1QEgzzhuRYh6m", "content": [{"title": "github.com", "url": "https://github.com/Glass-HQ/gpui"}, {"title": "gpui component", "url": "https://github.com/longbridge/gpui-component"}, {"title": "gpui kit", "url": "https://libraries.io/cargo/gpui-kit"}, {"title": "gpui framework", "url": "https://www.mintlify.com/Glass-HQ/Glass/reference/gpui-framework"}, {"title": "github.com", "url": "https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/blob/main/crates/gpui/README.md"}, {"title": "Expand description", "url": "https://docs.rs/gpui"}, {"title": "Expand description", "url": "https://docs.rs/gpui-pre/=0.3.7/"}, {"title": "guise-ui 1.0.0", "url": "https://docs.rs/crate/guise-ui/1.0.0"}, {"title": "Expand description", "url": "https://docs.rs/gpui-pre/=0.3.5/"}, {"title": "gpui.rs", "url": "https://gpui.rs/"}]}, "Based on the search results, here's what I found about GPUI:\n\n## Overview\n\nGPUI is a hybrid immediate and retained mode, GPU accelerated, UI framework for Rust, designed to support a wide variety of applications. It's a fast, productive UI framework for Rust from the creators of Zed.\n\n## Current Status\n\nGPUI is still in active development as we work on the Zed code editor, and is still pre-1.0. There will often be breaking changes between versions. You'll need to use the latest version of stable Rust and be on macOS or Linux.\n\n## Key Features\n\n- **Rendering**: GPUI is a custom GPU-accelerated UI framework that provides cross-platform rendering using Metal, DirectX, or Vulkan, reactive state management with entity-based architecture, and high performance with minimal allocations and efficient updates.\n\n- **Element Control**: Elements have total control over how they and their child elements are rendered and can be used for making efficient views into large lists, implement custom layouting for a code editor, and anything else you can think of.\n\n## Getting Started\n\nYou can create an application with Application::new(), and kick off your application by passing a callback to Application::run(). Inside this callback, you can create a new window with App::open_window(), and register your first root view.\n\nThere are also related frameworks and component libraries built on GPUI, such as GPUI Component and guise-ui, which provide additional pre-built UI components."], "durationSeconds": 5.968744792, "searchCount": 1}}
